      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-59711",
        "knowledge_point_id": "8f4e3599-287a-56a3-8f1b-9e7033803e0a",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying Acceleration on a Speed-Time Graph",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945962/assets/40143c20622029d70a978310a7d38bc41d7b8411151d3d5f61a3b280e5807841.png)\n\nThe speed-time graph shown above represents the motion of an object. At what times is the object accelerating?",
        "worked_solution": "The object is accelerating when its acceleration is positive. In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line. So, we need to find the times for which the slope is positive.\n\nWe see from the graph that the slope is positive from $t=0\\,\\text{s}$ to $t=30\\,\\text{s}.$ Therefore, the object is accelerating in this time interval.",
