        "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠B={60}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({60}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(x+2) & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\,x+2\\sqrt{3} & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x=2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2=4\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =x+2=2+2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
